1
00:00:05,367 --> 00:00:11,150
$10.5bn in hull premiums in 2025. About 112,500 vessels need cover every year.

2
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:16,533
Renewals go to those who stay in touch with owners all year.

3
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:21,750
Every vessel, owner group, insurer and renewal date on one screen.

4
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:26,650
One tap: the agent drafts a personal message.

5
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:32,033
Signals too: a newbuilding delivered, a vessel sold, a voyage into a war zone.

6
00:00:32,033 --> 00:00:37,442
Sales is a numbers game: 1% of 10,000 touches is about 100 placements.

7
00:00:37,442 --> 00:00:42,825
A personal cadence for every owner, every day, without a call-centre.

8
00:00:42,825 --> 00:00:47,358
WhatsApp, Telegram, WeChat and email in one feed.

9
00:00:47,358 --> 00:00:52,742
A master’s photo becomes text. A voice note becomes a transcript.

10
00:00:52,742 --> 00:00:57,275
Each owner has an AI agent that knows the whole history.

11
00:00:57,275 --> 00:01:02,658
It builds the renewal submission and finds what’s missing.

12
00:01:02,658 --> 00:01:07,192
Lead and following markets: rate, deductible, line and wording.

13
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:12,325
The agent counts the real cost, not just the rate.

14
00:01:12,325 --> 00:01:17,108
A master’s photo in WhatsApp becomes a claim file with a checklist.

15
00:01:17,108 --> 00:01:21,742
Great service today wins the renewal tomorrow.

16
00:01:21,742 --> 00:01:25,458
The agent suggests. You decide.

17
00:01:25,458 --> 00:01:30,092
Exactly the approved text goes out, and only once.

18
00:01:30,092 --> 00:01:36,225
Run the day by voice, in the car or at a conference: “Hey Siri, Pult.”

19
00:01:36,225 --> 00:01:40,958
Like aviation, marine insurance has a language every port understands.

20
00:01:40,958 --> 00:01:44,992
Few words, clear symbols. The agent speaks it, so your team does too.
